# Findings accepted for this project's stated scope -- a personal
# cost-controlled learning lab (CLAUDE.md principles 4-5), not a
# production environment. Each one below is a deliberate trade-off,
# not an oversight; several are already documented in-code or in an ADR.
# Re-evaluate if this project's threat model or budget ever changes.

# EKS control plane logging / secret encryption via KMS / public endpoint --
# same trade-off already documented inline on aws_eks_cluster.this
# (terraform/modules/eks/main.tf): kubectl from the operator's laptop
# without a bastion, kept simple on purpose for a single-operator lab.
AVD-AWS-0038
AVD-AWS-0039
AVD-AWS-0040
AVD-AWS-0041

# S3 SSE-S3 (AES256) over a customer-managed KMS key -- explicit decision
# in docs/adr/001-terraform-state-backend.md ("sem custo de KMS"), applied
# consistently to every bucket in this project, not just the state one.
AVD-AWS-0132

# ECR default encryption over a customer-managed KMS key -- same reasoning
# as AVD-AWS-0132, applied to the two ECR repositories.
AVD-AWS-0033

# Video bucket (terraform/envs/lab/s3.tf) is intentionally unversioned --
# ephemeral by design (force_destroy, torn down every session), unlike the
# state bucket, which is versioned.
AVD-AWS-0090

# No CloudFront WAF / access logging -- real ongoing cost (WAF ACL +
# per-request charges, extra S3 storage for logs) with no attacker model
# that justifies it for a personal lab behind its own domain.
AVD-AWS-0010
AVD-AWS-0011

# No S3 access logging (state or video bucket) -- extra storage cost for
# an audit trail CloudTrail already covers for a single operator.
s3-bucket-logging

# Public subnets legitimately assign public IPs (that's what makes them
# "public" -- NAT Gateway and the ALB need one) -- not a security lapse.
AVD-AWS-0164

# No VPC Flow Logs -- CloudWatch Logs ingestion cost with no compliance
# requirement for this project. Candidate for the observability stack if
# ever revisited (see CLAUDE.md "Próximos passos").
AVD-AWS-0178
